  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "Textual metaphor mapped onto historical figure",
  "description": "The text 'how do you like them well done please!' is an antisemitic metaphor that dehumanizes Jewish victims of the Holocaust by comparing their murder to cooking or eating food. This text is directly juxtaposed with the visual of Adolf Hitler, the historical figure responsible for orchestrating the Holocaust. The mapping implies that Hitler is being 'praised' or 'acknowledged' for his genocidal actions, with the text serving as a grotesque, hateful commentary on his role. The visual material (Adolf_Hitler) is mapped onto the textual metaphor (text_chunk) to create a disturbing analogy where the perpetrator is framed as the one who 'cooked' or 'done' the victims, thereby normalizing hatred and trivializing genocide.",
